# DTF tier manifest: repository-patch-clears-null  (artifact-keeper#4729, fixed by #5019; 1.12.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. Pure HTTP plus DB truth (docker exec psql)
# on one local generic repository. No mocks, no egress, no extra subnet.
#
# THE BUG
# PATCH /api/v1/repositories/{key} with {"description": null} or
# {"quota_bytes": null} answered 200 and changed nothing: both request fields
# were bare Option<_>, so an explicit null deserialized like an omitted field
# and the service's COALESCE($n, column) UPDATE kept the stored value. #5019
# gives both the three-way semantics project_id already has: omit to leave
# unchanged, null to clear (a NULL quota means unlimited), a value to set.
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) PATCH with values sets description and quota_bytes (response and
#             row); a PATCH that omits both (it only renames) leaves them
#             untouched; with a 1000-byte quota a 600-byte upload is admitted
#             and a second 600-byte upload is refused (413 at the session or
#             507 at complete). Green on both images.
#   (FIX)     {"quota_bytes": null} clears the quota (response and row) while
#             the omitted description stays; the 600-byte upload refused
#             before is then admitted. RED on 1.11.9 (quota stays 1000, upload
#             still refused).
#   (FIX)     {"description": null} clears the description (response and row)
#             while the omitted quota_bytes stays. RED on 1.11.9.
#   (FIX)     both fields null in one PATCH clear both. RED on 1.11.9.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one login plus about 20 back-to-back API calls.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
